# ML rules

- Split complete trips first, then create windows. Group route/driver/vehicle/phone when metadata permits.
- Fit feature normalization and calibration on training data only.
- TimesFM 3 is an optional desktop zero-shot baseline and teacher. No runtime package may import it.
- Always compare TimesFM with persistence, constant-velocity/turn-rate, filter prediction, TCN, and GRU baselines.
- Do not claim a TimesFM benefit without held-out effect size, tail metrics, calibration, and multiple trips/seeds.
- Teacher outputs for student training may be generated only inside training folds.
- Use causal feature windows. Any centered filter, backward fill, bidirectional network, or future-known covariate is prohibited in live metrics.
- Artificial blackout truth may exist only in the evaluator after inference.
- Record data hashes, splits, feature schema, configuration, seed, code commit, model hash, and hardware.
- Report per-trip rows, p50/p90/p95/worst case, and failure traces, not only global mean.
- Quantization needs accuracy and uncertainty-calibration revalidation.
- Export a compact independent ONNX student plus normalization metadata and schema hash.

